WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.067
Now the Arab League is

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.102
officially welcoming

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:04.037
a longtime international pariah

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:05.305
back into the fold.

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.107
It has re-admitted Syria

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:08.174
as a full member,

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.109
despite the government's

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:10.310
alleged war crimes

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.212
and an ongoing civil war.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.580
It's not a basher, reports

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.582
President Bashar al-Assad himself

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:16.950
could return to the spotlight

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.518
on the regional stage

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:20.920
as early as next week.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:24.024
An unthinkable prospect now

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:25.225
a reality

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:27.727
the Arab League has reinstated Syria

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.229
more than a decade

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:31.564
after Damascus was suspended over

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:32.432
President Bashar

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.099
al-Assad's

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.200
deadly crackdown

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.303
on anti-government protests.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:40.440
Now two of an Arab led political process

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.043
to end the bloody Syrian civil war

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:45.278
that has haunted the region for years.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:46.513
What we're talking

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:48.648
now is a political process

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:49.549
in which the Arabs

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.651
will have a leading role

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:52.318
in efforts

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.421
to try and bring about a solution to the

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:55.588
to the crisis.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:58.058
And in order for us to succeed,

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:00.660
we will all need to work together.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.929
Syria says it welcomed the announcement

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.597
and that it would participate

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.699
in strengthening joint Arab actions.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:08.668
The decision

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.670
to welcome Syria back into the fold

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.339
hasn't come as a total surprise.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:14.641
Following a series

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.709
of diplomatic victories for Assad

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.044
last week,

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.313
Iran's president, Ibrahim Razi,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.349
met with Assad in Damascus, a first

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:26.286
for an Iranian head of state in 13 years.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.088
And in April,

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:29.022
a similar visit

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:30.490
to the Syrian capital

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.559
by Saudi Arabia's foreign minister.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:36.362
But not all Arab states are supporting

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.831
Syria's return,

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:38.731
including some

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.800
that have actively supported Syria's

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.368
rebel groups.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:42.869
Qatar,

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.270
the minister of foreign affairs,

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:44.704
measured.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.406
But Mohamad al-Ansari

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:48.041
said his country continues

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:48.875
to stand against

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.643
the normalization of ties

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.912
with the Assad regime

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:55.081
and among those most wary of Syria's

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.116
a century.

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.317
Israel,

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.586
the IDF, suspected of hitting targets

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:00.954
inside Syria

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:03.323
to prevent Iran from gaining a foothold

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:05.191
as part of their proxy war.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:06.726
And for the

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:07.393
millions of

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.595
Syrian refugees

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.830
brutalized by Assad's war,

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.066
it may be hard to accept this decision

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:15.135
as anything but a betrayal

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.402
and a must have had them inhuman.

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.471
And this means nothing to us

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.772
because we are displaced

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.941
and forced to leave our towns.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:23.409
They are just like him.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.111
This is why they took him back.

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:27.347
They are all useless

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:28.648
Instead of Arab leaders

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:29.249
helping us

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:31.050
and getting us out of those camps

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.286
where we suffer and live in pain,

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:34.854
they whitewash the criminal

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:37.023
and killers hands from our blood.

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.727
President Assad could now participate

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.162
in the upcoming Arab League

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:43.062
summit in Saudi

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.130
Arabia,

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.165
though the league's secretary

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:46.866
general has been clear

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.301
this does not mean an end

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.336
to the Syrian crisis.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:50.837
With that,

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:53.273
I would add Syria in a shuttle market.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:54.741
The return of Syria

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:56.442
is the beginning of a movement

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:57.177
not an end.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.779
The direction of the resolution

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.714
to this crisis in Syria

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:03.183
will take time for procedures

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:05.318
to be implemented, and it will be gradual

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:07.587
shifting politics,

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:08.788
changing the landscape

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.223
of the Middle East,

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:11.624
but caught in the middle.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.626
Syrian refugees and citizens

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.162
still facing an uncertain future

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:19.666
with no clear indication of how or when

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:22.202
President Assad will be held to account.

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:25.605
Now the Bashir, CNN London

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.575
the US is criticizing

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:29.876
the Arab League's decision,

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.578
but some say the Biden administration

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:33.379
deserves criticism itself

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.347
for not doing enough

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:35.848
to stop the warming of ties

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.417
with Bashar al-Assad.

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:38.918
Our next guest signed an open

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:40.086
letter back in March

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:41.221
urging stronger

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.956
leadership on the Syrian issue.

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:44.557
Ambassador James Jeffrey

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.325
served as US

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:46.392
Special Representative

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:50.029
for Syria engagement from 2018 to 2020.

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.197
Ambassador, thank you

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:52.432
for joining us this evening.

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:55.668
Thank you for having me on.

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:58.071
So many will find this

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:00.540
an absolute betrayal of the Syrian people

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.841
and of course, the half a million or

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:04.444
so who've died as a result of this brutal

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.279
civil war.

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:07.981
But as Nadia was saying in her report,

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:09.515
there is not exactly coming

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:10.984
as a surprise.

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:13.353
Can you first explain to us, Ambassador,

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.388
as to the regional calculus

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:16.089
going on here

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:19.225
and why this is happening now?

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:22.061
First of all, this is both less

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:24.931
I would emphasize your report about what

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:27.166
the Arab League

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:28.501
president said

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:29.669
and also the other reports.

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:31.070
This is a beginning of a process.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:31.704
It's very slow.

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:32.772
So this is about less

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.307
than what it looks like

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:36.643
But in another sense, it's more

00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:38.611
since the late Obama administration

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.512
with John Kerry

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:41.881
through the Trump administration,

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:42.615
the U.S.

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.050
conducted negotiations

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.251
with Russia to achieve

00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:46.886
exactly what the Arab League is

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.188
now trying to do directly with Assad.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:50.690
That is to resolve

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.425
all of these problems that were covered

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:53.860
so well in your report.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.928
The Iranian dangerous presence

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.497
that Israel is striking,

00:04:57.497 --> 00:04:58.531
the various terrorist

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:58.998
groups

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:00.333
awash in Syria,

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:02.435
that we have troops there fighting.

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:03.870
The problem with refugees

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.438
the accountability of the regime,

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:07.240
the half a million people killed.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.908
These things are not going to be fixed

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:11.411
by Assad being in the Arab League.

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:12.645
They're not going to lift the U.S.

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:13.713
and European sanctions

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:16.215
they're not going to get Turkish and U.S.

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:17.583
troops out or Israeli

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:19.319
airplanes out of airspace.

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:22.155
That requires Assad to make compromises.

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:24.223
We have made that clear.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:24.957
Tony Blinken,

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.592
the secretary of state, called

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:28.594
the Jordanian foreign minister Safadi

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:29.362
on Thursday.

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:31.230
Safadi is the leader of this effort

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.333
to make it clear this how has to be done.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:36.336
Step by step, in accordance with the U.N.

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:37.637
resolution that covers

00:05:37.637 --> 00:05:38.871
all of these problems.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:40.073
So we have to wait and see.

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:41.808
This is not a revolutionary change.

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:43.142
It does show, however,

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:44.344
that the Arab states

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:45.845
are impatient with the U.S.

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:47.146
role at present in the region,

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:48.381
and that's troubling.

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:48.881
Yeah.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:49.415
So you are saying

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:50.550
that this has been on the table

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:53.019
really for some time with US involvement

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:56.322
Why then what prompted your letter,

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:58.324
your open letter to Joe Biden in March

00:05:58.591 --> 00:05:59.892
effectively saying that words

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:00.626
were not enough?

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:02.128
What other action

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:04.163
were you pushing for that?

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:05.932
Well, we were all aware

00:06:05.932 --> 00:06:07.100
of the Arab effort.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:09.569
Actually, King Abdullah announced it.

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:10.803
Jordan announced it

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:11.771
a year and a half ago,

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:13.673
and he delivered a version of it

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:15.441
to President Putin in Moscow.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:17.610
So this has been underway for some time.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.112
We're concerned

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:20.279
not that the Arabs

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:21.748
have the wrong approach,

00:06:21.748 --> 00:06:24.317
but the ability to carry it out.

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:27.854
Assad is a past master at deception.

00:06:27.854 --> 00:06:30.323
He has shown he will not compromise.

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:31.090
Our fear

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.960
is that if a committee of Arab leaders

00:06:34.127 --> 00:06:35.695
competing among themselves,

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:36.696
as they typically do

00:06:36.696 --> 00:06:38.431
on these things, tries

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:41.367
to get Assad to comply, it won't work.

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:42.368
And what's at stake

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:44.604
here is not just the refugees

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:46.172
for which we and others are providing

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:48.341
many billions of dollars a year.

00:06:48.341 --> 00:06:50.443
Are the terrorist groups or the fighting

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:51.811
that's still going on in Syria

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:53.546
This is a geopolitical issue.

00:06:53.546 --> 00:06:54.847
It involves a possible

00:06:54.847 --> 00:06:56.682
big win for Iran and Syria

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:57.283
and the region.

00:06:57.283 --> 00:06:58.818
The Arabs don't want that.

00:06:58.818 --> 00:07:00.052
They want to get a run out

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:01.587
and they want to get the region

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:03.423
in, particularly Syria, calm.

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:05.458
I'm just not sure they are the best

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:07.059
agent to do that.

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:09.061
Letter was United States.

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:10.430
You play a bigger role

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.265
instead We're apparently going

00:07:12.265 --> 00:07:14.033
to let the Arabs go ahead with this.

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:15.334
This may or may not work.

00:07:16.536 --> 00:07:17.937
So what are the

00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:18.938
what are the downsides here?

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:20.907
What are the pitfalls of this being led

00:07:20.907 --> 00:07:23.109
now by an Arab coalition?

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:24.477
And do the United States

00:07:24.477 --> 00:07:25.445
have any foothold

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:27.780
still to enter in at this late stage

00:07:27.914 --> 00:07:29.849
and influence proceedings?

00:07:29.849 --> 00:07:30.283
Oh, sure.

00:07:30.283 --> 00:07:31.384
Because you see that

00:07:31.384 --> 00:07:33.453
the things Assad wants,

00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:35.254
the Arab League and Arab states

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:36.656
cannot get it.

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:39.959
I would be very surprised if the Emiratis

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:41.093
or the Saudis or others

00:07:41.093 --> 00:07:43.296
are going to open their checkbooks

00:07:43.596 --> 00:07:46.933
and try to pay for the $400 billion

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:48.668
of destruction, mainly wrought

00:07:48.668 --> 00:07:49.936
by the Russians

00:07:49.936 --> 00:07:50.870
and the Iranians

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.972
on behalf of Assad inside Syria.

00:07:53.206 --> 00:07:55.041
There are strong U.S.

00:07:55.041 --> 00:07:56.409
and European sanctions.

00:07:56.409 --> 00:07:59.212
As I said, there are Turkish

00:07:59.212 --> 00:08:01.814
American and Israeli military forces

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:03.182
operating in Syria.

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:04.650
There is a third of the country

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:05.718
that's under the control

00:08:05.718 --> 00:08:06.819
still of one or another

00:08:06.819 --> 00:08:08.387
form of opposition groups.

00:08:08.387 --> 00:08:10.022
None of those things can be fixed

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:11.057
by the Arab League.

00:08:11.057 --> 00:08:11.991
Without these things

00:08:11.991 --> 00:08:13.960
being fixed and above all,

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:16.295
without a success to the U.N.

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:16.996
process.

00:08:16.996 --> 00:08:18.998
22 54 is a resolution.

00:08:19.432 --> 00:08:21.300
Assad isn't going to get very much,

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.835
and it's up to him

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:24.637
to start helping to fix these things.

00:08:24.637 --> 00:08:25.471
If he does,

00:08:25.471 --> 00:08:26.405
then this Arab League

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:28.741
initiative might have some progress

00:08:29.542 --> 00:08:30.142
Mean, the reality

00:08:30.142 --> 00:08:30.843
is, though, Ambassador,

00:08:30.843 --> 00:08:32.011
that this is now something

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:34.881
that's in motion. How important is it

00:08:35.982 --> 00:08:37.650
for those Arab allies to

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:39.552
try to exact a price from Assad

00:08:39.552 --> 00:08:41.521
in exchange for reintegration here?

00:08:41.521 --> 00:08:42.922
Do you think that is happening?

00:08:42.922 --> 00:08:45.091
And what should that exchange be?

00:08:46.259 --> 00:08:49.028
You've put your finger on the problem.

00:08:49.462 --> 00:08:50.630
Any diplomatic

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:52.265
you don't get any resolution

00:08:52.265 --> 00:08:53.533
to any international problem

00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:55.201
without a diplomatic process.

00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:56.802
But any diplomatic process

00:08:56.802 --> 00:08:59.238
tends to take on a life of its own.

00:08:59.505 --> 00:09:01.541
And the various participants

00:09:01.541 --> 00:09:04.810
want to save that process in the process

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.178
rather than the results

00:09:06.178 --> 00:09:07.313
you want to get on the ground,

00:09:07.313 --> 00:09:08.247
become the focus.

00:09:08.247 --> 00:09:09.448
That's what I'm afraid of.

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:11.851
What we told the Russians and they told

00:09:12.952 --> 00:09:14.987
the Syrian government,

00:09:14.987 --> 00:09:15.655
even though they didn't

00:09:15.655 --> 00:09:16.923
accept it, was, look,

00:09:16.923 --> 00:09:19.158
we want to do a step by step resolution.

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:20.159
Essentially, the plan

00:09:20.159 --> 00:09:21.027
that the Arabs are now

00:09:21.027 --> 00:09:21.928
putting on the table.

00:09:21.928 --> 00:09:23.563
But if not, we'll be happy

00:09:23.563 --> 00:09:25.131
to freeze this conflict

00:09:25.131 --> 00:09:26.799
and continue on with our sanctions

00:09:26.799 --> 00:09:27.466
and continue on

00:09:27.466 --> 00:09:28.734
with our military presence,

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:30.202
as we believe the Turks

00:09:30.202 --> 00:09:30.870
and the Israelis

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.739
will also do until you actually comply,

00:09:34.674 --> 00:09:35.608
because we saw this

00:09:35.608 --> 00:09:37.043
as a geostrategic problem.

00:09:37.043 --> 00:09:39.512
I'm not sure the Arabs will be that tough

00:09:39.679 --> 00:09:40.680
if they yield,

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.916
if they start taking paper promises and

00:09:44.951 --> 00:09:46.052
insignificant

00:09:46.052 --> 00:09:48.955
concessions on Assad spots as enough,

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:51.123
they'll simply put pressure on us,

00:09:51.123 --> 00:09:53.192
the Europeans, the Turks and the Israelis

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:55.161
to start making our own concessions.

00:09:55.161 --> 00:09:56.696
That's riskier.

00:09:56.696 --> 00:09:57.830
So important.

00:09:57.830 --> 00:09:58.431
Ambassador, here,

00:09:58.431 --> 00:09:59.732
this context in light of

00:09:59.732 --> 00:10:01.567
what is emerging here.

00:10:01.567 --> 00:10:02.668
Thank you so much for coming

00:10:02.668 --> 00:10:03.936
on, giving us your insight on this.

00:10:03.936 --> 00:10:05.371
We appreciate it.

00:10:05.738 --> 00:10:07.206
Thanks for having me.

00:10:07.206 --> 00:10:08.107
Thank you.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:09.275
Now we're just learning

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:10.142
about an alleged

00:10:10.142 --> 00:10:11.777
smuggling operation by Iran

00:10:11.777 --> 00:10:13.813
to get weapons into Syria.

00:10:13.813 --> 00:10:15.114
This according to an Israeli

00:10:15.114 --> 00:10:15.982
defense official

00:10:15.982 --> 00:10:17.583
and two sources familiar with U.S.

00:10:17.583 --> 00:10:18.451
intelligence.

00:10:18.451 --> 00:10:19.952
They say Iran used

00:10:19.952 --> 00:10:21.821
humanitarian aid shipments

00:10:21.821 --> 00:10:22.822
as a cover

00:10:22.822 --> 00:10:24.991
after a devastating earthquake in Syria

00:10:24.991 --> 00:10:25.958
in February.

00:10:25.958 --> 00:10:27.159
The sources say Iran

00:10:27.159 --> 00:10:28.995
hid weapons and military equipment

00:10:28.995 --> 00:10:31.030
among humanitarian supplies

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:32.765
that were transported by

00:10:32.765 --> 00:10:34.433
convoys through Iraq.

